.TH HOSTAGES 6 "October 2026" "hostages" "Games"
.SH NAME
hostages \- port of the Amiga version of Hostages (Infogrames, 1988)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hostages
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIdisk.adf\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the original Amiga Hostages executables on an emulated A500. The game
disk image is not redistributable and must be supplied by the user.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-paths
Print resolved data and save directories and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-save \fIDIR\fR, \-\-user\-data\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Directory for the written disk image and save states
(default: $XDG_STATE_HOME/hostages on Linux).
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Extra search root for ADF images.
.TP
.B \-\-scale \fIN\fR
Window scale factor (default 3).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help.
.SH FILES
Writable state is stored under the save directory (written ADF copy and
.I states/
slots). ADF images are searched in the current directory,
.IR assets/ ,
and the install data directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
.I https://github.com/Grumbel/hostages-port
